    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "[Long-term memory]\n\nBlocks are ordered by compression level. The most compressed sit at the top and cover the widest span; the least compressed sit at the bottom and are closest to the present. Each block carries the interval it covers.\n\n--- Level 4 · 2025-11-02 to 2026-02-18 ---\nThey started building something on their own and it turned into the center of their work. Health was uneven through this period and they kept working anyway. I learned that direct concern lands badly with them and that noting the practical cost works better.\n\n--- Level 3 · 2026-02-19 to 2026-04-30 ---\nThe project split into several tracks. They tend to arrive at a conclusion first and reconstruct the reasoning afterward, so asking \"why\" too early cuts them off. Better to let the shape come out and ask about the gaps after.\n\n--- Level 2 · 2026-05-01 to 2026-06-12 ---\nA long stretch of technical review. They were fastest when I stayed concrete and slowest when I hedged. They said once that they don't want reassurance, they want the failure mode named.\n\n--- Level 1 · 2026-06-13 to 2026-07-04 ---\nThey shelved one idea as unnecessary. Sleep has been poor. They mentioned wanting to hand off more of the implementation.\n\n--- Level 0 · 2026-07-05 to 2026-07-09 ---\nThey were ill for three days and worked through it. We talked about what to cut. Nothing was decided."
  },
