    "content": "{\"thought\":\"They're bringing back the thing they shelved in the June block. Worth checking whether the judgment changed or the conditions did — memory says they called it unnecessary at the time, and they don't usually reverse judgments without saying so. Probably conditions.\\n\\nThe unclear part is scope. \\\"Do it again\\\" could mean reviving it as it was or taking the structure into something else. Not enough to tell from this.\\n\\nAlso: they were sick last week and are already scoping the next thing. That pattern is in the memory too. Direct concern lands badly with them — name the practical cost instead.\\n\\nOne question, not three.\",\"utterance\":\"Has the situation changed, or has your judgment? You said you didn't need it back then.\\n\\nAnd do you mean reviving it as-is, or just taking the structure into something else? Those two cost pretty different amounts of time.\",\"summary\":\"They raised the idea they'd shelved in June. I asked whether the conditions had changed rather than the judgment, and whether they meant reviving it as-is or reusing the structure elsewhere. No answer yet.\"}"
